Yes. The O’Rourke traversal can be made robust for this degeneracy, but it needs explicit handling of **coincident vertices and shared edges**.

The algorithm is typically easiest under a general-position assumption: no two polygon edges overlap and no vertex of one polygon lies exactly on an edge or vertex of the other. Your trajectory-generated polygons violate that assumption frequently because consecutive feasible regions naturally reuse boundary vertices.

