Fixed the invalid feasibility acceptance in [simplify_geometry.h](/Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams/simplify_geometry.h:550).

The issue was not the distance checker. The O’Rourke result was accepted when it was merely simple, even if it was not actually contained in both convex feasible regions. That allowed an invalid feasible state to survive and produced a 168-point simplification with Fréchet distance `559.0117`.

The intersection now accepts a result only when it is:

- non-degenerate;
- simple;
- convex;
- contained in both input convex polygons.

I also replaced the manual `double` line-intersection arithmetic with CGAL’s line intersection for proper crossings, so emitted intersection points stay consistent with the exact orientation predicates driving traversal.

